      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027ve previously talked about this under the assumption that this has to be done in 5 weeks, but with the extended timeline (January IC and 100% coverage by end of March), I think it might make sense to convert these tests to Kotlin. We have increasingly been using Kotlin in tests as it offers many features that make tests much easier to develop and more readable. If you\u0027re up for the challenge (I promise you\u0027ll get the hang of it in no time!) I would highly encourage you to do so. I\u0027ll leave it up to you though.\n\nCheck out [EthernetManagerTest](https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Connectivity/tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/EthernetManagerTest.kt;l\u003d604?q\u003dethernetmanagertest) which are written in Kotlin and I believe are very readable (though I might be somewhat biased).",
      "revId": "7e25df56915793d228665ecd5f50089f5d83ab1e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
